   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["diagramAmplitude", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Evaluate the expression associated with one generated diagram.",
   "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"diagramAmplitude", "[", "diagram",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ",
     "Return one diagram's bare amplitude expression."}], "Usage"],
  Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["This lower-level singular function \
returns only the expression. For a process, use diagramAmplitudes, which \
retains each diagram's mass rules with its expression.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Constructive evaluation combines internal photon or gluon helicities \
and expands external x factors. Known mass replacements are applied before \
return.", "Notes"], Cell["Feynman evaluation retains ordered Dirac chains, \
Lorentz and color tensors, and off-shell internal lines. Convert Feynman \
tensors through the dedicated Feynman tools or preparation workflow.",
   "Notes"], Cell["A single diagram generally is neither reference \
independent nor a complete amplitude. Its simplification may need completion \
after diagrams are combined.", "Notes"], Cell["Examples",
   "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
         "\"ConstructiveDiagrams`\"", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ", "Get", "[",
         "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "Global`$HEPCATpath", ",", " ",
         "\"HEPCAT.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]", ";", "\n", "hepcatDirectory",
         " ", "=", " ", "ParentDirectory", "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]",
         ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[",
         "{", "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"models\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n",
         "feynmanModelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"model_feynman\"", "}", "]", ";"}]],
      "Input", InitializationCell -> True]}, Open]],
  Cell["Basic Examples", "ExampleSection"],
  Cell["Inspect the first constructive diagram expression.", "ExampleText"],
